  "final_message": "The sensor dashboard is built, but I haven't built the Docker image or run the app under gunicorn.\n\nWhat I did run:\n- **Frontend:** `tsc --noEmit` is clean and `npm run build` succeeds.\n- **API:** I ran the backend through Flask's test client and it behaved as expected.\n  - Duplicate usernames, with the check ignoring case, get 409.\n  - Posting a sensor without a token gets 401.\n  - A non-owner trying to delete someone else's sensor gets 403.\n  - A non-numeric reading value gets 400.\n  - Deleting your own sensor gets 204, and a later `GET` on it gets 404.\n  - `GET /api/sensors` sorts by name and `last_value` updates after a reading.\n  - The readings list returns newest first with the correct `total`.\n\nI didn't test the frontend in a browser.\n\nDesign choices:\n- **Backend:** All routes are in `backend/app.py`, with data in `data/sensors.db`. Login tokens are random, stored hashed and expire after 30 days.\n- **Frontend:** The chart is hand-drawn SVG, not a charting library. Both the dashboard and the sensor page refresh every 10 seconds.\n- **Extra endpoints:** I added `/api/auth/me` and `/api/auth/logout` for the signed-in username and the sign-out button. They weren't in your spec.\n- **Reading limit:** `GET .../readings` returns 100 readings by default and at most 1000, and the sensor page asks for 50.\n- **New dependencies:** I added Tailwind (`tailwindcss`, `@tailwindcss/vite`), TypeScript and the React type packages to `frontend/package.json`, and updated the lock file. I also added a `tsconfig.json`, a `typecheck` npm script and a `.gitignore`.",
